ORMS Annual Meeting will be held at the Georgia World Congress Center and the Omni Atlanta Hotel at Centennial Park in Atlanta, Georgia, and it runs from October 26-28, 2025.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain specific information about the facility layout, placement details, or industrial track session locations. To find more detailed information about the facility layout and industrial track session placements, you may want to:\n\n1. Visit the official 2025 INFORMS Annual Meeting website directly at meetings.informs.org/wordpress/annual2025/\n2. Check the agenda page at meetings.informs.org/wordpress/annual2025/agenda/ for session details\n3. Contact the INFORMS conference organizers directly through their official website\n\nThe search results indicate that detailed agenda and session information is available online, but the specific facility layout and industrial track placement details are not included in these particular search results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b5f5aa5f-f7b4-4947-a8e8-e68cc2cb9ebd","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:26.013Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6838ca2c-fc2f-4053-9f4c-4fff2358335b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"861c32fd-48ab-4e2d-a980-741eab3c2c3a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a0a1880745aab67e3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NUCbNPKCAkb5UFyHszy86N","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CPAIOR 2025 industrial track case study CP-SAT large scale\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CPAIOR Conference Series\",\"url\":\"https://cpaior.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR 2025\",\"url\":\"https://sites.google.com/view/cpaior2025\"},{\"title\":\"Program\",\"url\":\"https://cpaior.github.io/cpaior_2025/program.html\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR: Integration of AI and OR Techniques in Constraint Programming 2027 2026 2025 ...\",\"url\":\"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/program?id=574\"},{\"title\":\"Theory Announcements: [DMANET] [CPAIOR 2025] — Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://dmatheorynet.blogspot.com/2024/09/dmanet-cpaior-2025-call-for-papers.html\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR 2025 : Integration of AI and OR Techniques in Constraint Programming\",\"url\":\"https://callforpaper.org/cfp/cpaior-2025-integration-of-ai-and-or-techniques-in-constraint-programming_227\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR 2025 | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=cpaior.org/CPAIOR/2025\"},{\"title\":\"[CPAIOR 2025] — Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/isaim/c/-zsNiQty_N8\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR 2025 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://sites.google.com/view/cpaior2025/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR 2025 : Integration of AI and OR Techniques in Constraint Programming\",\"url\":\"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/servlet/event.showcfp?eventid=182533&copyownerid=106070\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found information about CPAIOR 2025, though the specific details about an industrial track case study using CP-SAT on large-scale problems were not explicitly detailed in these results.\n\nHere's what I found:\n\nCPAIOR 2025 is the 22nd International Conference on the Integration of Constraint Programming, Artificial Intelligence, and Operations Research, held in Melbourne, Australia from November 10 to November 13, 2025.\n\nThe conference aims to bring together researchers from Constraint Programming (CP), Artificial Intelligence (AI), and Operations Research (OR) to present new techniques or applications, with a main objective of showing how the integration of techniques from different fields can lead to interesting results on large and complex problems.\n\nThe conference strongly encourages regular papers or experience reports showcasing CP/AI/OR techniques on challenging real-world applications.\n\nHowever, the search results did not contain specific information about an industrial track case study involving CP-SAT and large-scale problems. To find more detailed information about this specific topic, you may want to visit the official CPAIOR 2025 website or check the detailed program once it's published.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"226eada1-265b-4d62-b266-32aaab8251a7","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:28.564Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"861c32fd-48ab-4e2d-a980-741eab3c2c3a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"15beb2b8-3199-4886-8985-77a30ac7e594","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a0a1880745aab67e3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017pMV6ev1CcCPvQjuC2AXLu","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EURO Conference 2025 OR facility layout case study industrial application\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Facility layout and supply chain management of food service industries: A case study | IEEE Conference Publication | IEEE Xplore\",\"url\":\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9600088\"},{\"title\":\"MCDM Model for Evaluating and Selecting the Optimal Facility Layout Design: A Case Study on Railcar Manufacturing\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2227-9717/11/3/869\"},{\"title\":\"Full article: Smarter facility layout design: leveraging worker localisation data to minimise travel time and alleviate congestion\",\"url\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/00207543.2024.2374847\"},{\"title\":\"EURO 2025 in Leeds\",\"url\":\"https://www.gams.com/campaign/euro_2025/\"},{\"title\":\"EURO 2025\",\"url\":\"https://www.gams.com/conferences/2025-06-euro_leeds-uk/\"},{\"title\":\"Call for Papers (Publish with DOI) – IEOM Paris, July 2-4, 2025: 8th European Industrial Engineering and Operations Management Conference | INFORMS Open Forum\",\"url\":\"https://connect.informs.org/discussion/call-for-papers-publish-with-doi-ieom-paris-july-2-4-2025-8th-european-industrial-engineering-and-operations-management-conference\"},{\"title\":\"CASE STUDIES | Industrial Management and Engineering Group\",\"url\":\"https://www.imegllc.com/case-studies/\"},{\"title\":\"EURO 2025 | ORS\",\"url\":\"https://www.theorsociety.com/ORS/ORS/Events/2025/EURO-2025/EURO-2025.aspx\"},{\"title\":\"CASE Europe Annual Conference 2025 | CASE\",\"url\":\"https://www.case.org/conferences-training/case-europe-annual-conference-2025\"},{\"title\":\"Layout Design for a Low Capacity Manufacturing Line: A Case Study - Filippo De Carlo, Maria Antonietta Arleo, Orlando Borgia, Mario Tucci, 2013\",\"url\":\"https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.5772/56883\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search for \"EURO Conference 2025 facility layout case study industrial application\". Here are the relevant findings:\n\n## EURO 2025 Conference\n\nThe 34th European Conference on Operational Research (EURO) will take place from June 22 to June 25, 2025, at the University of Leeds in the United Kingdom, celebrating the 50th Anniversary of the Association of European Operational Research Societies.\n\nThe \"Making an Impact\" stream at EURO Leeds 2025 focuses on case studies that solve real problems and deliver observable outcomes, with discussions and workshops addressing practical challenges of implementation in Operational Research, Analytics and Data Science.\n\n## Facility Layout Case Studies and Industrial Applications\n\nThe search results reveal several relevant case studies on facility layout design in industrial settings:\n\n1. **Railcar Manufacturing**: A study proposes a Fuzzy Analytic Hierarchy Process (F-AHP) with Fuzzy TOPSIS method for determining ideal layouts, with results from a railcar industrial case study indicating the model can effectively lead to selection of the most suitable facility layout.\n\n2. **Assembly Line Application**: A real-world case study involving a tricycle assembly line with six workers and seven facilities demonstrated the potential to reduce travel time by a minimum of 32% and alleviate congestion.\n\n3. **Fashion Manufacturing**: A comparison of different layout design methods for low-volume batch fashion manufacturing lines analyzed a manufacturing line of felt hats.\n\nThese topics align well with the operational research and practical industrial optimization themes of the EURO 2025 conference.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"0d78c085-a3f4-470a-9846-ff8015b164d4","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:30.127Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"15beb2b8-3199-4886-8985-77a30ac7e594","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e04da5d9-cf37-4a3d-9697-68fb62b2390b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a0a1880745aab67e3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017JExqoCKKqqQZ8J8q73h76","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Gurobi case study facility layout warehouse placement large scale 2024\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Facility Location Example Problem - Gurobi Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.gurobi.com/jupyter_models/facility-location-example-gurobi/\"},{\"title\":\"Facility Location Problem Demo - Gurobi Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.gurobi.com/resources/facility-location-problem-demo/\"},{\"title\":\"Facility Location | Gurobi Modeling Examples\",\"url\":\"https://gurobi.github.io/modeling-examples/facility_location/\"},{\"title\":\"Facility location problems — Mathematical Optimization: Solving Problems using Gurobi and Python\",\"url\":\"https://scipbook.readthedocs.io/en/latest/flp.html\"},{\"title\":\"modeling-examples/facility_location/facility_location.ipynb at master · Gurobi/modeling-examples\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Gurobi/modeling-examples/blob/master/facility_location/facility_location.ipynb\"},{\"title\":\"modeling-examples/facility_location/README.md at master · Gurobi/modeling-examples\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Gurobi/modeling-examples/blob/master/facility_location/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"Facility Examples - Gurobi Example Tour\",\"url\":\"https://docs.gurobi.com/projects/examples/en/current/examples/facility.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - HarshavardhanV/Warehouse-location-and-optimization-Case-Study-Using-Gurobi-and-python-: In this the overall problem is solved using python and Gurobi.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/HarshavardhanV/Warehouse-location-and-optimization-Case-Study-Using-Gurobi-and-python-\"},{\"title\":\"Warehouse-location-and-optimization-Case-Study-Using-Gurobi-and-python-/Problem description.txt at master · HarshavardhanV/Warehouse-location-and-optimization-Case-Study-Using-Gurobi-and-python-\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/HarshavardhanV/Warehouse-location-and-optimization-Case-Study-Using-Gurobi-and-python-/blob/master/Problem%20description.txt\"},{\"title\":\"Facility Location Problem Demo | Gurobi\",\"url\":\"https://www.gurobi.com/resources/demos/facility-location-problem-demo\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found several Gurobi case studies and resources related to facility layout and warehouse placement problems:\n\n## Main Gurobi Case Studies\n\nGurobi provides an example showing how to tackle a facility location problem that involves determining the number and location of warehouses that are needed to supply a group of supermarkets.\n\nThe key case study scenario involves a large supermarket chain in the UK needing to build warehouses for a set of supermarkets opening in Northern England, where the locations of the supermarkets have been decided, but decisions must be made regarding how many warehouses to open and at which candidate locations to build them.\n\n## Problem Structure\n\nThe optimization challenge involves finding the optimal tradeoff: opening many warehouses would reduce the average distance a truck has to drive from the warehouse to the supermarket and reduce delivery cost, but opening a warehouse has a fixed cost associated with it.\n\n## Methodology\n\nGurobi demonstrates how to construct a mixed-integer programming (MIP) model of this problem, implement this model in the Gurobi Python API, and then use the Gurobi Optimizer to find an optimal solution.\n\n## Industry Applications\n\nThe techniques are applicable across multiple industries including retail and e-commerce (warehouse and fulfillment center location), manufacturing (factory location), and telecommunications (network tower positioning).\n\nThere's also a community case study on GitHub that addresses a constraint where at least 80% of demand (by tons) must be satisfied by a facility within 500 miles of the customer, with the goal of finding the minimum number of warehouses that will satisfy this constraint.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"868fbfae-78b3-4893-9bd0-4df602ee047b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:30.693Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e04da5d9-cf37-4a3d-9697-68fb62b2390b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
