{"parentUuid":"60577e43-8db3-4bfd-a3a3-d8eff5a45f47","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a0a1880745aab67e3","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_016YPVH7jhYyZT8AYcobD6h1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Wcvg488DLLWVYhoEZJnjEF","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"cell manufacturing layout automotive case study large scale MIP solver runtime"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5525,"cache_read_input_tokens":26360,"output_tokens":324,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5525},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":324,"cache_read_input_tokens":26360,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5525,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5525,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caot7syQTBndQbyx67DQ4","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"2bb596e7-282d-4501-a73a-aed9d318e18a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:50.961Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c71040eb-3878-453c-8f5e-46da3e904875","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a0a1880745aab67e3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AdE2qTKBfPzJzVaqePDSGF","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Hexaly\" OR \"LocalSolver\" facility layout 2D packing case study Decathlon Bouygues\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Hexaly\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/\"},{\"title\":\"New release: LocalSolver 12.0\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/announcement/new-release-localsolver-12-0\"},{\"title\":\"Solvers for Scheduling and Routing Problems |\",\"url\":\"https://dmcommunity.org/2024/04/16/localsolver-is-now-hexaly/\"},{\"title\":\"LocalSolver 8.0 — Hexaly 13.0 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/last/changelog/localsolver80.html?redirect\"},{\"title\":\"LocalSolver 7.0 — Hexaly 14.0 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/last/changelog/localsolver70.html\"},{\"title\":\"Migrate from LocalSolver to Hexaly — Hexaly 14.5 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/last/changelog/migration.html\"},{\"title\":\"Hexaly on LinkedIn: How LocalSolver efficiently solves network design problems for Bouygues…\",\"url\":\"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/hexaly_how-localsolver-efficiently-solves-network-activity-7092051331858763776-so6W?trk=public_profile_like_view\"},{\"title\":\"Localsolver - Crunchbase Company Profile & Funding\",\"url\":\"https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/localsolver\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) LocalSolver 1.x: A black-box local-search solver for 0-1 programming\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220340267_LocalSolver_1x_A_black-box_local-search_solver_for_0-1_programming\"},{\"title\":\"Shape optimization through Simulation Optimization with LocalSolver - Hexaly\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/tutorial/shape-optimization-through-simulation-optimization-with-localsolver?redirect\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about Hexaly (formerly LocalSolver) and its relationship with Bouygues, though the specific case study mentioning facility layout and 2D packing with both Decathlon and Bouygues was not found in these results.\n\nHere's what I found:\n\n**About Hexaly and LocalSolver:**\nLocalSolver has been renamed to Hexaly which claims to be the world's fastest optimization solver for Routing, Scheduling, and Packing problems. Since November 2023, LocalSolver has become Hexaly. This new name is intended to better reflect what our solver has become, moving progressively from a solver based on local search techniques to a global optimization solver, combining numerous optimization techniques.\n\n**Connection to Bouygues:**\nThe search results show a Bouygues connection, though focused on network design rather than facility layout. Bouygues Telecom's network engineering team has used LocalSolver's optimization solution since 2014. It enabled the company to connect 3,000 new nodes and the ones they already operated.\n\nAdditionally, T. Benoist, F. Gardi, R. Megel extend special thanks to Dr. Etienne Gaudin, director of Bouygues e-lab, for his support and encouragements. in the early LocalSolver research paper.\n\nThe specific case study combining facility layout, 2D packing, Decathlon, and Bouygues was not found in these search results. You may want to search the Hexaly or LocalSolver website directly or contact their team for this specific case study.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b4ddee76-777c-447f-9969-c372627c2abe","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:56.000Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c71040eb-3878-453c-8f5e-46da3e904875","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"7a43d714-9751-47c1-b67e-27dca4903382","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a0a1880745aab67e3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AdZgZg24zCA9DxZ7VLVcMj","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"INFORMS Journal on Computing\" 2024 2025 large scale facility layout MILP decomposition\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Asymptotically Tight MILP Approximations for a Nonconvex QCP | INFORMS Journal on Computing\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/ijoc.2024.0719\"},{\"title\":\"Algorithms for Hybrid MILP/CP Models for a Class of Optimization Problems | INFORMS Journal on Computing\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/ijoc.13.4.258.9733\"},{\"title\":\"Exact MILP Models for Redundancy Allocation with Mixed Components | INFORMS Journal on Computing\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/ijoc.2024.0842\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - INFORMSJoC/2024.0755\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/INFORMSJoC/2024.0755\"},{\"title\":\"Articles in Advance | INFORMS Journal on Computing\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/toc/ijoc/0/0\"},{\"title\":\"Layout Optimization for a Large-Scale Grid-Connected Solar Power Plant | INFORMS Journal on Computing\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/ijoc.2023.0223\"},{\"title\":\"Current Issue | INFORMS Journal on Computing - PubsOnLine\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/toc/ijoc/current\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - INFORMSJoC/2023.0059\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/INFORMSJoC/2023.0059\"},{\"title\":\"Redesigning Benders Decomposition for Large-Scale Facility Location | Management Science\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/abs/10.1287/mnsc.2016.2461\"},{\"title\":\"Multi commodity network design problem with minimum flow constraints\",\"url\":\"https://ideas.repec.org/a/eee/oprepe/v15y2025ics2214716025000351.html\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found a highly relevant article from the INFORMS Journal on Computing that matches your query:\n\n\"Layout Optimization for a Large-Scale Grid-Connected Solar Power Plant\" by Chong Wang, Qinghua Wu, Kai Pan, and Zuo-Jun Max Shen was published in INFORMS Journal on Computing in 2024 (Volume 37, Issue 6, pages 1560-1586).\n\nThis paper addresses large-scale layout optimization using MILP and decomposition methods. The paper focuses on layout planning of a solar power plant involving complex optimization problems such as district partitioning, photovoltaic component location, and cable routing, and addresses the integrated location and routing (ILR) problem. \n\nThe authors develop exact algorithms to solve the ILR problem via a decomposition framework (a variant of Benders decomposition) and develop an exact branch-and-cut scheme to solve each subproblem in the decomposition framework. Their decomposition method achieves an average gap of 0.02% between the obtained lower and upper bounds.\n\nThis appears to be the paper most closely matching your search query combining INFORMS Journal on Computing, 2024, large-scale facility layout problems, and MILP decomposition techniques.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"53d2300e-d5ba-4d1f-a4c9-c3269929a7cf","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:56.154Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7a43d714-9751-47c1-b67e-27dca4903382","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"60577e43-8db3-4bfd-a3a3-d8eff5a45f47","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a0a1880745aab67e3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0175qznJxerSoo29pGJGm22H","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Alibaba JD warehouse slotting layout optimization paper KDD 2024\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Warehouse Management Optimization Using A Sorting- ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.jiem.org/index.php/jiem/article/download/5661/1075\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Warehouse Management Optimization using a Sorting-Based Slotting Approach\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/378307142_Warehouse_Management_Optimization_using_a_Sorting-Based_Slotting_Approach\"},{\"title\":\"Layout optimization of irregular storage areas under class storage strategy based on clustering and multi-bin size packing problem - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11364414/\"},{\"title\":\"Warehouse Layout Optimization: Techniques for Improved Order Fulfillment Efficiency | International Journal of Acta Informatica\",\"url\":\"https://yuktabpublisher.com/index.php/IJAI/article/view/135\"},{\"title\":\"Warehouse Optimisation in 2025 | PerformanSC\",\"url\":\"https://performansc.com/news/warehouse-optimisation/\"},{\"title\":\"Frontiers | A novel framework for automated warehouse layout generation\",\"url\":\"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/artificial-intelligence/articles/10.3389/frai.2024.1465186/full\"},{\"title\":\"Trends and new practical applications for warehouse allocation and layout design: a literature review | Discover Applied Sciences | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s42452-023-05608-0\"},{\"title\":\"Slotting Optimization Model for a Warehouse with Divisible First-Level Accommodation Locations\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2076-3417/11/3/936\"},{\"title\":\"A novel framework for automated warehouse layout generation - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11518846/\"},{\"title\":\"Second Place Overall Solution for Amazon KDD Cup 2024\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=OEjXPwR7aE\"}]\n\nThe search results don't contain information about a specific Alibaba JD warehouse slotting layout optimization paper presented at KDD 2024. The results show various general papers on warehouse optimization and slotting strategies, but none specifically match your query about an Alibaba/JD collaboration paper at the KDD 2024 conference.\n\nThe only KDD 2024-related result found was about an Amazon KDD Cup 2024 competition (which is different from the main KDD conference track).\n\nIf you're looking for a specific academic paper on warehouse optimization from Alibaba or JD.com presented at KDD 2024, you may want to:\n\n1. Check the official KDD 2024 proceedings directly\n2. Search for it on academic databases like ACM Digital Library (KDD is an ACM conference)\n3. Look on arXiv for preprints from 2024\n4. Check the companies' research pages directly\n\nWould you like me to search for more specific information, such as by looking for Alibaba or JD papers on warehouse optimization at KDD 2024 more broadly?\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"318058f9-8a21-44c9-916f-d02d0c4eff1a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:56.914Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"60577e43-8db3-4bfd-a3a3-d8eff5a45f47","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"2bb596e7-282d-4501-a73a-aed9d318e18a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a0a1880745aab67e3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wcvg488DLLWVYhoEZJnjEF","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"cell manufacturing layout automotive case study large scale MIP solver runtime\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Production system configuration and layout planning for efficient manufacturing system design: An industrial case study - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1755581726000143\"},{\"title\":\"Cell formation and layout design using genetic algorithm and TOPSIS: A case study of Hydraulic Industries State Company - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10763945/\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Facility and Process Layout Analysis of an SME using Simulation: A Case Study of a Manufacturing Company\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/316737994_Facility_and_Process_Layout_Analysis_of_an_SME_using_Simulation_A_Case_Study_of_a_Manufacturing_Company\"},{\"title\":\"An improved algorithm for layout design in cellular manufacturing systems - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S027861251000021X\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Cellular Manufacturing Layout Design in Inner Tube Manufacturing Industry : A Case Study\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/8482130/Cellular_Manufacturing_Layout_Design_in_Inner_Tube_Manufacturing_Industry_A_Case_Study\"},{\"title\":\"Optimizing Cellular Manufacturing Facility Layout Design ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.clausiuspress.com/assets/default/article/2023/06/14/article_1686731246.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Cellular Layout Optimization Case Study\",\"url\":\"https://www.imegllc.com/cellular-layout-optimization/\"},{\"title\":\"An integrated approach for the cell formation and layout design in cellular manufacturing systems | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/263371658_An_integrated_approach_for_the_cell_formation_and_layout_design_in_cellular_manufacturing_systems\"},{\"title\":\"A grid-aware MIP solver: Implementation and case studies - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0167739X07000520\"},{\"title\":\"IBM ILOG CPLEX Optimization Studio\",\"url\":\"https://www.ibm.com/products/ilog-cplex-optimization-studio\"}]\n\nI've found several relevant case studies and research papers on cell manufacturing layout design with MIP solver approaches. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Automotive Case Study with MIP Solvers\n\nA production system configuration and layout planning study for an industrial automotive case implemented MILP models using FICO Xpress. The research compared a \"Baseline method\" and \"Advanced method,\" with the advanced method demonstrating superior performance in terms of number of optimal solutions and average running times across different problem sizes.\n\n## Large-Scale MIP Problem Solving\n\nResearch has introduced comprehensive Mixed-Integer Linear Programming (MILP) models to solve integrated cell formation and layout problems, with hybrid approaches including Simulated Annealing Linear Programming (SALP) and Genetic Algorithm Linear Programming (GALP) developed to solve large-scale issues.\n\n## Solver Runtime Performance\n\nOne study found that their proposed approach achieved a 33.25% better layout score and solved the problem 116.64% faster than a MINLP model solved via Gurobi's standard solver. A simulated annealing-based algorithm produced solutions with better quality and less computation time compared to benchmarked algorithms, with computation time advantages being particularly significant as problem size increases.\n\nThe research indicates that cell formation and layout problems have exponential complexity in computation time, making them NP-hard problems, which is why advanced solver techniques and hybrid approaches are commonly employed for large-scale automotive manufacturing scenarios.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ff80ea33-86eb-458d-ab01-acbf28fd141d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:58.632Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2bb596e7-282d-4501-a73a-aed9d318e18a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
