{"parentUuid":"d8ad919c-ec5e-41c3-8f4d-04020c066061","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a0a1880745aab67e3","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_014a43Ld19V18HMX2BFg6pyT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PbZNQCGWABeW8GF3qQXBCm","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://sites.google.com/view/cpaior2024/accepted-papers","prompt":"List all accepted papers at CPAIOR 2024, especially any with industrial application, facility layout, placement, packing, large-scale, or Benders decomposition themes. Include authors and titles."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5401,"cache_read_input_tokens":31885,"output_tokens":405,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5401},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":405,"cache_read_input_tokens":31885,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5401,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5401,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caot8tmJss4rxaYWZ4w5v","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"90ea151f-8ac1-4216-9b4e-632f80aadfeb","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:01:05.979Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"53b8f3ba-1f6e-40c7-b09d-5c85f8e5bf8e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a0a1880745aab67e3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BpYzczaxfKhfWgzxPmUg95","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"OR-Tools\" CP-SAT industrial case study Google production scheduling 2024\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"Industrial-size job shop scheduling with constraint programming - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2214716022000215\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/docs/scheduling.md at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/docs/scheduling.md\"},{\"title\":\"Constraint Optimization | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT solver (Job Shop Scheduling): Add Worker constraint & PK to data\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/vkOMUojl7EM\"},{\"title\":\"Student Scheduling CP-SAT Precedence · google/or-tools · Discussion #2286\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/2286\"},{\"title\":\"Optimization problems and Google OR-Tools | by Mohammad Nazari | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@mnazari/optimization-problems-and-google-or-tools-6197fc39e073\"}]\n\nI found relevant search results about OR-Tools CP-SAT and industrial scheduling. Here's what I discovered:\n\n## Key Findings\n\nOR-Tools is an open-source solver developed by Google and a recurrent winner of the MiniZinc Challenge. \n\nThe most relevant industrial case study I found is a research paper that elaborates the performance of state-of-the-art constraint solvers with respect to industrial-size job shop scheduling problem instances. This study compares the performance of two cutting-edge constraint solvers: OR-Tools, an open-source solver developed by Google and recurrent winner of the MiniZinc Challenge, and CP Optimizer, a proprietary constraint solver from IBM targeted at industrial optimization problems.\n\nThe research used realistic benchmark scenarios where benchmarks comprise up to one million operations to be scheduled on up to one thousand machines, reflecting real-world industrial scenarios with heavy workloads like those found in the semi-conductor domain.\n\nThe paper is from August 2022, which is close to but not exactly 2024. CP has been successfully applied in planning, scheduling, and numerous other domains with heterogeneous constraints, and the CP method is a powerful tool for solving large, real-world scheduling problems.\n\nUnfortunately, I did not find a specific Google case study from 2024 in these results. The industrial job shop scheduling study appears to be the most comprehensive case study comparing OR-Tools CP-SAT on large-scale production scheduling problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ab22cacc-e0d0-4036-9b79-ff1d9127d223","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:01:09.286Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"53b8f3ba-1f6e-40c7-b09d-5c85f8e5bf8e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e35628ba-e809-430f-a2b0-7292d7fbe3ed","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a0a1880745aab67e3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wbjdkcxkps4Tq4BAdxUcWR","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"container loading\" 3D bin packing industrial case Maersk DHL solver case study\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - skjolber/3d-bin-container-packing: A variant of the Largest Area Fit First (LAFF) algorithm + brute force algorithm · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/skjolber/3d-bin-container-packing\"},{\"title\":\"Solving a 3D bin packing problem with stacking constraints - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0360835223008380\"},{\"title\":\"A three-dimensional container loading algorithm for solving logistics packing problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2192437625000160\"},{\"title\":\"bin packing problem - an efficiency analysis between ...\",\"url\":\"https://scholars.unh.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=2875&context=thesis\"},{\"title\":\"Thinking Inside the Box: How to Solve the Bin Packing Problem with Ray on Databricks | Databricks Blog\",\"url\":\"https://www.databricks.com/blog/thinking-inside-box-how-solve-bin-packing-problem-ray-databricks\"},{\"title\":\"A layer-building algorithm for the three-dimensional multiple bin packing problem: a case study in an automotive company - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2405896315003687\"},{\"title\":\"3DPACK.ING | AI-Powered 3D Container & Truck Loading Calculator & Packing Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://3dpack.ing/\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A genetic algorithm for the three-dimensional bin packing problem with heterogeneous bins\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/273121476_A_genetic_algorithm_for_the_three-dimensional_bin_packing_problem_with_heterogeneous_bins\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) An Online Packing Heuristic for the Three-Dimensional Container Loading Problem in Dynamic Environments and the Physical Internet\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/315638765_An_Online_Packing_Heuristic_for_the_Three-Dimensional_Container_Loading_Problem_in_Dynamic_Environments_and_the_Physical_Internet\"},{\"title\":\"A three-dimensional container loading algorithm for solving logistics packing problem - R Discovery\",\"url\":\"https://discovery.researcher.life/article/a-three-dimensional-container-loading-algorithm-for-solving-logistics-packing-problem/209568abea6f3f92bb9a2ba5c58a1613\"}]\n\nI've performed a web search for container loading and 3D bin packing industrial applications. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Industrial Applications and Algorithms\n\nA two-stage method was developed for addressing a novel industrial 3D bin packing problem that incorporates stacking constraints, with testing on weakly heterogeneous industrial instances using ISO containers with standard dimensions of 587 × 233 × 220.\n\n## Solver Approaches\n\nThe mathematical solver used was Gurobi 9.0.2, and a branch-and-price algorithm was introduced specifically designed to solve stack packing problems.\n\n## Significant Performance Improvements\n\nThe adoption of the 3D bin packing algorithm marks a significant advancement, offering a solution that is not only more accurate but also considerably faster, reducing the time required for container selection by a factor of 40x as compared to legacy processes.\n\n## Broader Industry Context\n\nIn shipping and transportation industry, several types of standard containers with different dimensions are used. For marine transport, standard containers of 20 or 40 feet length are used.\n\nWhile the search results show extensive research on 3D bin packing for container loading, I did not find specific case studies explicitly attributed to Maersk or DHL in these results. The research demonstrates that 3D bin packing solvers are widely used in logistics and industrial applications, with significant performance improvements over legacy methods.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"44b1ffcb-91cc-479e-be32-7a17c54afe48","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:01:09.916Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e35628ba-e809-430f-a2b0-7292d7fbe3ed","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d8ad919c-ec5e-41c3-8f4d-04020c066061","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c7a9c836-fcfa-483d-8466-444dc60bbf86","agentId":"a0a1880745aab67e3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014UcVURp99N9PhJPiosKcHA","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"INFORMS 2024\" OR \"INFORMS 2025\" Amazon FedEx Walmart talk warehouse network design\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Five Lessons from Walmart’s Strategic Network Design Talk for my Students\",\"url\":\"https://miketalksai.substack.com/p/five-lessons-from-walmarts-strategic\"},{\"title\":\"Regionalize and Scale: Amazon’s Fulfillment Network Design for Faster and Cheaper Delivery | INFORMS Journal on Applied Analytics\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/inte.2025.0295\"},{\"title\":\"Warehouse-Retailer Network Design Problem | Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/opre.1030.0096\"},{\"title\":\"The distribution network of Amazon and the footprint of freight digitalization - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7419283/\"},{\"title\":\"Introducing Amazon Supply Chain Services: Amazon’s logistics network, now open to every business\",\"url\":\"https://www.aboutamazon.com/news/retail/amazon-supply-chain-services-for-business\"},{\"title\":\"‘It’s not just all the big companies’: Warehouse robotics use expands | Supply Chain Dive\",\"url\":\"https://www.supplychaindive.com/news/warehouse-robotics-adoption-increases-supply-chains/812369/\"},{\"title\":\"Amazon adds Walmart, Shopify, Shein to Multi-Channel Fulfillment coverage | Supply Chain Dive\",\"url\":\"https://www.supplychaindive.com/news/amazon-walmart-shopify-shein-multi-channel-fulfillment/760392/\"},{\"title\":\"Amazon takes aim at the supply chain\",\"url\":\"https://www.axios.com/2026/05/05/amazon-logistics-ups-fedex\"},{\"title\":\"Amazon opens China distribution center for US-bound seller inventory | Supply Chain Dive\",\"url\":\"https://www.supplychaindive.com/news/amazon-opens-china-distribution-center-for-us-bound-seller-inventory/817806/\"},{\"title\":\"Walmart introduces Walmart Fulfillment Services: Walmart’s response to Amazon’s FBA program - Rithum\",\"url\":\"https://www.rithum.com/blog/walmart-introduces-walmart-fulfillment-services-walmarts-response-to-amazons-fba-program/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about warehouse network design talks at INFORMS conferences:\n\nWalmart gave a great talk on strategic supply chain network optimization at the 2024 INFORMS conference. Walmart is redesigning its ambient (room temperature) supply chain by determining the long-term strategy for replacing two types of warehouses (manual RDCs and High Velocity DCs) with new automated facilities that can handle all products. This work won the INFORMS Edelman Prize.\n\nWalmart's talk covered five different types of problems they were solving, including traditional network design and transition planning for the ambient network, eCommerce product flow, reducing empty miles from 50% to 33%, vehicle routing for home delivery options from stores, and affinity planning.\n\nAdditionally, I found information about Amazon's fulfillment network design strategy, which addresses regionalization to maximize benefits of regional fulfillment while balancing shipment-level costs and consolidation opportunities.\n\nThe search results did not contain specific information about FedEx talks at INFORMS 2024 or 2025 regarding warehouse network design, but they do show active work by all three companies on logistics and supply chain optimization.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"aba3919d-76e2-4bbf-9a33-915a759bbfc4","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:01:10.788Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d8ad919c-ec5e-41c3-8f4d-04020c066061","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"90ea151f-8ac1-4216-9b4e-632f80aadfeb","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c7a9c836-fcfa-483d-8466-444dc60bbf86","agentId":"a0a1880745aab67e3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PbZNQCGWABeW8GF3qQXBCm","type":"tool_result","content":"# CPAIOR 2024 Accepted Papers with Industrial/Operational Themes\n\n## Industrial Application & Logistics\n\n**\"Online optimization of a dial-and-ride problem with the integral primal simplex\"** by Elahe Amiri, Antoine Legrain, and Issmaïl El Hallaoui addresses real-time transportation optimization challenges.\n\n**\"A Constraint Programming Approach for Aircraft Disassembly Scheduling\"** by Charles Thomas and Pierre Schaus tackles aerospace manufacturing logistics.\n\n**\"ULD Build-Up Scheduling with Logic-Based Benders Decomposition\"** by Ricardo Euler, Ralf Borndoerfer, Christian Puchert, and Tuomo Takkula applies decomposition methods to airline cargo operations.\n\n**\"A Constraint Programming Model for the Electric Bus Assignment Problem with Parking Constraints\"** by Mathis Azema, Guy Desaulniers, Jorge Mendoza, and Gilles Pesant addresses transit fleet management.\n\n**\"Acquiring Constraints for a Non-linear Transmission Maintenance Scheduling Problem\"** by Hugo Barral et al. focuses on electrical grid maintenance optimization.\n\n## Large-Scale Applications\n\n**\"Strategies for Compressing the Pareto Frontier: Application to Strategic Planning of Hydropower in the Amazon Basin\"** by Zhongdi Qu et al. demonstrates large-scale infrastructure planning using multi-objective optimization techniques.\n\n## Note\n\nWhile several papers employ Benders decomposition methodologically, only the ULD scheduling paper explicitly titles it as a core technique."}]},"uuid":"c6eddde1-cf27-406d-9829-3ee75af86a1b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:01:12.571Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"90ea151f-8ac1-4216-9b4e-632f80aadfeb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","session