{"parentUuid":"12ab085b-4c21-46a8-9918-b7c07106d2d0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c7a9c836-fcfa-483d-8466-444dc60bbf86","agentId":"a0a1880745aab67e3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E8ETCGFVXb6NVxN1Eq7qHF","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"job shop\" scheduling industrial 2024 case study Bosch Siemens Renault million operations CP-SAT\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Industrial-size job shop scheduling with constraint programming - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2214716022000215\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Scheduling job shop - A case study\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/307900214_Scheduling_job_shop_-_A_case_study\"},{\"title\":\"Industrial Size Job Shop Scheduling Tackled by Present Day CP Solvers | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-30048-7_9\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Optimization of Job Shop Scheduling Problem Using Genetic Algorithm and Simulated Annealing: A Case Study of Manufacturing Industry\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/387361581_Optimization_of_Job_Shop_Scheduling_Problem_Using_Genetic_Algorithm_and_Simulated_Annealing_A_Case_Study_of_Manufacturing_Industry\"},{\"title\":\"Case Study Analysis of Job Shop Scheduling and its Integration with Material Requirement Planning - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S2214785319310387\"},{\"title\":\"Job shop planning and scheduling of reconfigurable manufacturing systems | Operations Management Research | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s12063-025-00551-2\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Digital-Twin-Based Job Shop Scheduling Toward Smart Manufacturing\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/335510620_Digital-Twin-Based_Job_Shop_Scheduling_Toward_Smart_Manufacturing\"},{\"title\":\"A Study of Flexible Job-Shop Scheduling with Dual Constraints\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2227-9717/12/12/2649\"},{\"title\":\"Job shop scheduling - Cornell University Computational Optimization Open Textbook - Optimization Wiki\",\"url\":\"https://optimization.cbe.cornell.edu/index.php?title=Job_shop_scheduling\"},{\"title\":\"A survey of job shop scheduling problem: The types and models - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0305054822000338\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about industrial-size job shop scheduling with constraint programming:\n\nResearch using novel benchmarks comprises up to one million operations to be scheduled on up to one thousand machines to reflect real-world industrial scenarios with heavy workloads like found in the semi-conductor domain. Developments during the last decade improved the performance of state-of-the-art constraint solvers dramatically, to the point that they can be applied also on large-scale instances.\n\nAdditionally, research aims to close gaps by testing the capabilities of the best available CP solvers on job shop scheduling problems, targeting not only classic benchmarks from the literature but also a new benchmark of large-scale instances reflecting nowadays industrial scenarios.\n\nHowever, I should note that while the search results discuss industrial-size job shop scheduling with constraint programming approaches and mention benchmarks with millions of operations, the specific case studies mentioning Bosch, Siemens, and Renault with CP-SAT solver were not found in these particular search results. The results focus more on the general approaches and benchmark creation for such industrial problems rather than specific named case studies.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"1e4c9d3c-27d8-4fee-a115-f46d4bf64c93","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:01:36.904Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"12ab085b-4c21-46a8-9918-b7c07